{
    "word": "intrepidity",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "a36a00cc-706c-3646-937f-06702e132786",
                "word": "intrepidity",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "4f1d7e90-ba20-463f-90a7-bcac664009fb",
                        "entry_id": "a36a00cc-706c-3646-937f-06702e132786",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "intrepidities"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2123c61b-a04e-3e9c-a2a3-cff697eda696",
                        "entry_id": "a36a00cc-706c-3646-937f-06702e132786",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The quality of being intrepid; bravery."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0fbfda63-414a-4a83-9c2b-bb0b0dca4a54",
                                "sense_id": "2123c61b-a04e-3e9c-a2a3-cff697eda696",
                                "text": "[…] Pipes, who acted as the enemy's forlorn hope, advanced to the gate with great intrepidity, and clapping his foot to the door, which was none of the ſtouteſt, with the execution and diſpatch of a petard, ſplit it into a thouſand pieces."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f88b273-e9ea-4d96-8012-9c5ec7624afc",
                                "sense_id": "2123c61b-a04e-3e9c-a2a3-cff697eda696",
                                "text": "Miss Bingley immediately fixed her eyes on his face, and desired he would tell her what lady had the credit of inspiring such reflections. Mr. Darcy replied with great intrepidity, \"Miss Elizabeth Bennet.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "49a72826-02cf-4849-9a3e-7ca6689c5d0c",
                                "sense_id": "2123c61b-a04e-3e9c-a2a3-cff697eda696",
                                "text": "The pale, inscrutable determinateness, and flinchless intrepidity of Pierre, now began to domineer upon them; for any social unusualness or greatness is sometimes most impressive in the retrospect."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a2b6e27-d5c6-478d-899e-a8796ea6ec1f",
                                "sense_id": "2123c61b-a04e-3e9c-a2a3-cff697eda696",
                                "text": "And then I think I saw the most tremendous exhibition of moral courage and intrepidity that it is possible to conceive."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d272a082-250a-4d8b-9ec6-e84f7e4bbce3",
                                "sense_id": "2123c61b-a04e-3e9c-a2a3-cff697eda696",
                                "text": "[T]here are common and covert ones [dangers], that \"look like nothing\" and that can be but inwardly and occultly dealt with, which involve the sharpest hazards to life and honour and the highest instant decisions and intrepidities of action."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "00ed477d-7bf6-4968-a314-452b17fac459",
                        "source_entry_id": "a36a00cc-706c-3646-937f-06702e132786",
                        "source_sense_id": "2123c61b-a04e-3e9c-a2a3-cff697eda696",
                        "source_sense_description": "bravery",
                        "target_lang_word": "intrépidité",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "intrépidité",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a81b6056-7571-3e93-a714-8d9dc9ab671b",
                                        "entry_id": "6d8e2522-dba5-3c0b-8cc6-a7283cfb6a5b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fermeté inébranlable dans le péril."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea9bcb13-5c97-43b3-a213-8708af295a24",
                                                "sense_id": "a81b6056-7571-3e93-a714-8d9dc9ab671b",
                                                "text": "Il a fait preuve d’intrépidité, d’une grande intrépidité."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1bd5d373-9ec1-4859-b538-71330b022bce",
                                                "sense_id": "a81b6056-7571-3e93-a714-8d9dc9ab671b",
                                                "text": "Il avait arraché ses galons sur le front grâce à une intrépidité remarquable."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1b34d4b1-82fd-4116-b30c-d31f58de308d",
                        "source_entry_id": "a36a00cc-706c-3646-937f-06702e132786",
                        "source_sense_id": "2123c61b-a04e-3e9c-a2a3-cff697eda696",
                        "source_sense_description": "bravery",
                        "target_lang_word": "bravoure",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bravoure",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6a4cc247-eae3-3ef3-8ee1-42fbeaf90a3b",
                                        "entry_id": "812c2004-ef60-3ccc-899d-26427f3973b2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Courage guerrier ; vaillance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "812ce7e7-f027-4eed-bdac-73d9d32d709a",
                                                "sense_id": "6a4cc247-eae3-3ef3-8ee1-42fbeaf90a3b",
                                                "text": "Sa figure, une de celles que la bravoure a marquées de son cachet, offrait le type que cherche aujourd'hui l'artiste quand il songe à représenter un des héros de la France impériale."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6994e8d7-0f36-4702-8e7b-c0d39b5215ff",
                                                "sense_id": "6a4cc247-eae3-3ef3-8ee1-42fbeaf90a3b",
                                                "text": "Il avait plus de cran au front. Il était même très brave, d'une bravoure innocente."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5eee191c-c487-4d8a-b170-2bbc9854ffb5",
                                                "sense_id": "6a4cc247-eae3-3ef3-8ee1-42fbeaf90a3b",
                                                "text": "Certes, Jean-Luc en tira l’avantage essentiel en utilisant ses talents de conteur qui transformaient en acte de bravoure sa fuite devant les policiers. Mais il eut le bon goût de m’associer dans le récit de son épopée."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba5d75ac-3c85-4e99-afbe-b0ffe18b42c5",
                                                "sense_id": "6a4cc247-eae3-3ef3-8ee1-42fbeaf90a3b",
                                                "text": "Cependant jamais soldats ne méritèrent plus d'être victorieux ; ceux de la brigade d’Austrasie, surtout, donnèrent l'exemple de la plus grande bravoure : […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
